(The part is a large automotive bumper fascia: a 1.69 m organic Class-A shell \(492/498 B-spline faces\) with a thin, near-uniform ~2.5 mm) Tj
T* (wall and a fill ratio of 0.0036 confirming a hollow moulded shell — this is classic large-part injection moulding. Resin is undecided from) Tj
T* (geometry; I selected PP Impact Copolymer \(PP-B\) as the industry-standard bumper fascia material \(impact-tough, low cost, paintable\),) Tj
T* (with PC/ABS as the higher-stiffness alternative. Net part weight in PP is 2.163 kg. Projected area \(10,946.8 cm²\) and wall \(2.5 mm\) are) Tj
T* (used verbatim per the deterministic rules. At 200,000/yr a single large-cavity dedicated tool is appropriate; mould cost ~£200k. Main risks) Tj
T* (are the 4 undercuts/2 zero-draft faces needing side actions, the very high flow-length-to-wall ratio, and warpage/weld-line cosmetics on) Tj
T* (the painted surface. Manufacturability score fixed at 53.) Tj
